# Line endings
# ------------
# Normalise everything to LF inside the repository, and let Git check files out
# with the platform's native endings. Declaring this explicitly is what stops
# Git guessing per-file — the guessing is what produced the endless
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it" warnings.
#
# Those warnings come from core.safecrlf, which fires whenever a round-trip
# conversion would not be byte-identical. They are advisory only; nothing was
# ever at risk. To silence them completely, also run once:
#
#     git config core.safecrlf false

* text=auto

# Files that must keep LF regardless of platform
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.php       text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.xml       text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
.gitignore  text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Never touch these
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.zip       binary
